 ],
 "literal": "Our afflicted-they-indeed, O chief of the agricultural tract, front yard / bud mature puṉku tree's flower fallen white sand / Vēlaṉ decorated veṟi dance performing ground every / red paddy white puffed grain scattered like / sand dune reached our town's wide ghat / beautiful joints forearm holding / with the celestial nymphs made oath indeed.",
 "translation": "O chief of the agricultural tract! The oath you took, holding her beautiful-jointed forearm, swearing by the celestial nymphs at the wide ghat of our town near the sand dunes—where the fallen flowers of the puṉku tree with mature buds lie on the white sand of the front yard, looking like white puffed red-paddy grains scattered across every ground decorated by the Vēlaṉ priest for the veṟi dance—has indeed afflicted us.",
 "modern": "மகிழ்நனே! அரும்புகள் முதிர்ந்த புன்க மரத்தின் மலர்கள் உதிர்ந்து கிடக்கும் முன்றிலின் வெண்மணல், வேலன் அலங்கரித்த வெறியாடும் களங்களிலெல்லாம் தூவப்பட்ட செந்நெல்லின் வெண்மையான பொரியைப் போலக் காட்சி அளிக்கும். அத்தகைய மணல்மேடுகள் நிறைந்த நம் ஊரின் அகன்ற துறையிலே, அவளுடைய அழகிய மணிக்கட்டையுடைய முன் கையைப் பற்றி, அணங்கு போன்ற தெய்வ மகளிர் முன்னிலையில் நீ செய்த சூளுரை எங்களை மிகவும் வருத்துகிறது.",
 "explanation": "The friend of the heroine is speaking to the hero who has returned from his visits to courtesans. She reminds him of the solemn oath he once took at the wide river-ghat of their town, holding the heroine's hand and swearing by the celestial nymphs that he would never leave her. Now that he has broken that promise, that very oath has come back to haunt and afflict them. The white sand of the front yard is covered with fallen white flowers of the puṉku tree, resembling the white puffed rice scattered in the worship grounds of the Vēlaṉ priest. This image of ritual worship and sacred spaces reinforces the solemn, religious nature of the oath he took, making his betrayal of it even more painful. Key words include makiḻṉa (chief of the agricultural tract), cūḷ (oath), aramakaḷir (celestial nymphs), and aṇaṅkiṉavē (they afflicted).",
